IMPORT prelude

-- Hostage-Taking Act 2010 (Singapore) -- the hostage-taking offence and its two punishment limbs (ss 2, 3), extraterritoriality
-- (s 4), the duty to disclose information (s 5), the Public Prosecutor's bank-freeze, inspection and information orders and the
-- offences for not complying (ss 6, 7, 8), consent to prosecute (s 9), protection of informers (s 10), liability of officers and
-- partners (s 11), arrest without warrant (s 12) and the extradition deeming (s 14(1)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HTA2010.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 17 of 2022 (in force 1 July 2022) shown on s 14.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 10 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. The Act is short (14 sections), so most of it is
-- encoded. Not encoded: s 13 and s 14(2) to (8) (mutual assistance and the Gazette notifications applying the Extradition Act 1968
-- to Convention countries) beyond the flat deemings, the meaning of "customer information" (borrowed from s 40A of the Banking Act
-- 1970), the content of a s 8(1) order, and rules under s 11(7) for foreign entities.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Hostage-Taking Act 2010 -- offences and powers`

§§ `2 -- hostage-taking offence`

-- s 2: "hostage-taking offence" means "(a) the offence under section 3; or (b) an abetment of, or a conspiracy or attempt to commit,
-- the offence under section 3".
DECLARE Involvement IS ONE OF
    `committing the s 3 offence`
    `abetting it`
    `conspiring to commit it`
    `attempting it`
    `harbouring the offender afterwards`

GIVEN `the involvement` IS AN Involvement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the involvement is a hostage-taking offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the involvement`
    WHEN `harbouring the offender afterwards` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 -- hostage-taking`

-- s 3(1): any person (A) who "(a) seizes or detains another person (B); and (b) threatens to cause death or hurt to B or to continue
-- to detain B, or by A's conduct gives rise to a reasonable apprehension that B may be put to death or hurt or may continue to be
-- detained, or causes death or hurt to B, in order to compel -- (c) the Government, the government of another State or an
-- international intergovernmental organisation to do or abstain from doing any act ... shall be punished with death or imprisonment
-- for life, and shall, if A is not sentenced to death, also be liable to fine or to caning; or (d) any other person (C) to do or
-- abstain from doing any act ... shall be punished with imprisonment for a term which may extend to 15 years, and shall also be
-- liable to fine or to caning."
-- s 3(2): subsection (1) "does not apply to any act which is an offence under section 3 of the Geneva Conventions Act 1973".
DECLARE Incident HAS
    `A seized or detained B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `A threatened death, hurt or continued detention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `A's conduct gave a reasonable apprehension of death, hurt or continued detention` IS A BOOLEAN
    `A caused death or hurt to B` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to compel a government or intergovernmental organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `to compel any other person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an offence under s 3 of the Geneva Conventions Act 1973` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is a coercive element` IF
        `the incident`'s `A threatened death, hurt or continued detention`
    OR  `the incident`'s `A's conduct gave a reasonable apprehension of death, hurt or continued detention`
    OR  `the incident`'s `A caused death or hurt to B`

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the incident is an offence under s 3` IF
        `the incident`'s `A seized or detained B`
    AND `there is a coercive element` `the incident`
    AND (    `the incident`'s `to compel a government or intergovernmental organisation`
         OR  `the incident`'s `to compel any other person`)
    AND (NOT `the incident`'s `an offence under s 3 of the Geneva Conventions Act 1973`)

-- Which limb punishes. INFERENCE: where A means to compel both a government and a private person, the text does not say which limb
-- applies; this encoding takes limb (c), since the act is then done "in order to compel" a government.
DECLARE Punishment IS ONE OF
    `death or imprisonment for life, and fine or caning if not sentenced to death`
    `imprisonment up to 15 years, and fine or caning`
    `no s 3 punishment`

GIVEN `the incident` IS AN Incident
GIVETH A Punishment
`the s 3 punishment` MEANS
    IF NOT `the incident is an offence under s 3` `the incident`
    THEN `no s 3 punishment`
    ELSE IF `the incident`'s `to compel a government or intergovernmental organisation`
         THEN `death or imprisonment for life, and fine or caning if not sentenced to death`
         ELSE `imprisonment up to 15 years, and fine or caning`

§§ `4 -- extraterritoriality`

-- s 4: "Every person who, outside Singapore, commits an act that, if committed in Singapore, would constitute a hostage-taking
-- offence is deemed to commit the act in Singapore and may be proceeded against, charged, tried and punished accordingly."
-- No nationality or residence condition is stated.
GIVEN `would be a hostage-taking offence in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `committed outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `the offender is a Singapore citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act may be tried in Singapore` IF
    `would be a hostage-taking offence in Singapore`

§§ `5 -- duty to disclose information`

-- s 5(1): "Every person in Singapore who has information which he or she knows or believes may be of material assistance -- (a) in
-- preventing the commission by another person of a hostage-taking offence; or (b) in securing the apprehension, prosecution or
-- conviction of another person, in Singapore, for a hostage-taking offence, and who fails to disclose the information immediately to
-- a police officer shall be guilty of an offence" -- fine up to $50,000 or imprisonment up to 5 years or both.
-- (2), (3): good-faith disclosure attracts no criminal or civil proceedings and breaches no restriction imposed by "law, contract or
-- rules of professional conduct". No reasonable-excuse defence is written into s 5(1).
DECLARE Knowledge HAS
    `the person is in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows or believes it may materially help prevent another's hostage-taking offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knows or believes it may materially help secure another's apprehension, prosecution or conviction in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disclosed it immediately to a police officer` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the knowledge` IS A Knowledge
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to disclose is an offence under s 5` IF
        `the knowledge`'s `the person is in Singapore`
    AND (    `the knowledge`'s `knows or believes it may materially help prevent another's hostage-taking offence`
         OR  `the knowledge`'s `knows or believes it may materially help secure another's apprehension, prosecution or conviction in Singapore`)
    AND (NOT `the knowledge`'s `disclosed it immediately to a police officer`)

GIVEN `disclosed under s 5` IS A BOOLEAN, `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discloser is protected from proceedings and from breach of confidence` IF
    `disclosed under s 5` AND `in good faith`

§§ `6 -- freezing a bank account`

-- s 6(1): the Public Prosecutor, if satisfied that ransom money "may be paid out of any account with any bank", may by order direct
-- the bank not to pay out of the account "for a specified period not exceeding one month". (2) A complying bank "is relieved of any
-- liability to any other person in respect of the payment prohibited". (3) A non-complying bank: fine up to $20,000.
-- INFERENCE: "one month" is read as the calendar month running from the order, supplied as its length in days.
GIVEN `the specified period in days` IS A NUMBER, `the calendar month in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the freeze period is within s 6(1)` IF
        `the specified period in days` GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the specified period in days` AT MOST `the calendar month in days`

GIVEN `under a s 6 order` IS A BOOLEAN, `the bank refused the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the bank is relieved of liability for refusing the payment` IF
    `under a s 6 order` AND `the bank refused the payment`

§§ `7 -- inspection of customer information`

-- s 7(1): the Public Prosecutor may, if evidence of a hostage-taking offence (or a s 4 act) by a person "is likely to be found in any
-- document containing customer information relating to that person, to the spouse, son or daughter of that person or to a person
-- reasonably believed by the Public Prosecutor to be a trustee or agent for that person", authorise "any police officer of or above
-- the rank of assistant superintendent" to inspect the bank's documents.
-- (4) The power may be delegated to a Deputy Public Prosecutor or the Commissioner of Police, "except the power of delegation".
DECLARE Relation IS ONE OF
    `the suspect`
    `the suspect's spouse`
    `the suspect's son`
    `the suspect's daughter`
    `a person believed to be the suspect's trustee or agent`
    `the suspect's parent`
    `the suspect's sibling`

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `customer information about this person may ground a s 7 order` IF
    CONSIDER `the relation`
    WHEN `the suspect's parent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the suspect's sibling` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Rank IS ONE OF
    `sergeant`
    `inspector`
    `assistant superintendent`
    `deputy superintendent`
    `superintendent`

GIVEN `the rank` IS A Rank
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an officer of this rank may be authorised to inspect` IF
    CONSIDER `the rank`
    WHEN `sergeant` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `inspector` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Delegate IS ONE OF
    `a Deputy Public Prosecutor`
    `the Commissioner of Police`
    `an assistant superintendent`

GIVEN `the delegate` IS A Delegate, `delegating the power to delegate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the s 7 delegation is valid` IF
        (NOT `delegating the power to delegate`)
    AND CONSIDER `the delegate`
        WHEN `an assistant superintendent` THEN FALSE
        OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 7(3): "Any person who, without reasonable excuse, fails to produce any document demanded by the police officer which is in his
-- or her possession or control" -- fine up to $20,000 or imprisonment up to 2 years or both.
GIVEN `the document was in the person's possession or control` IS A BOOLEAN, `produced it on demand` IS A BOOLEAN, `had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to produce is an offence under s 7(3)` IF
        `the document was in the person's possession or control`
    AND (NOT `produced it on demand`)
    AND (NOT `had a reasonable excuse`)

§§ `8 -- orders to furnish information`

-- s 8(1): the Public Prosecutor may by order require (a), (b) the person to furnish sworn statements of property; (c) any other person
-- to do so; (d) the Comptroller of Income Tax to furnish information; (e) the head of a ministry, department or statutory board to
-- furnish documents; (f) a bank to give copies of accounts.
-- (2) Every recipient must comply "despite any obligation of secrecy imposed under any written law or rule of law".
-- (3) Subsection (2) does not apply to a person in (1)(e) if the responsible Minister "certifies that it would be against the
-- interests of national security" for the contents to be disclosed.
-- (5) Contravening (2): fine up to $20,000 or imprisonment up to 2 years or both. No reasonable-excuse defence is written in.
-- (6) Furnishing information "known to him or her to be false or misleading in a material particular": the same.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the person under investigation`
    `any other person`
    `the Comptroller of Income Tax`
    `the head of a ministry, department or statutory board`
    `a bank`

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `the Minister certified a national security objection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient must comply with the s 8 order` IF
    CONSIDER `the recipient`
    WHEN `the head of a ministry, department or statutory board` THEN NOT `the Minister certified a national security objection`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the recipient` IS A Recipient, `the Minister certified a national security objection` IS A BOOLEAN, `complied in time` IS A BOOLEAN, `bound by a secrecy obligation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `non-compliance is an offence under s 8(5)` IF
        `the recipient must comply with the s 8 order` `the recipient` `the Minister certified a national security objection`
    AND (NOT `complied in time`)

GIVEN `in purported compliance with a s 8 order` IS A BOOLEAN, `false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN, `known to be so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `furnishing it is an offence under s 8(6)` IF
    `in purported compliance with a s 8 order` AND `false or misleading in a material particular` AND `known to be so`

§§ `Penalties for the offences other than s 3`

-- ss 5(1), 6(3), 7(3), 8(5), 8(6). The s 6(3) offence (a bank) carries a fine only.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `s 5 failing to disclose information`
    `s 6(3) bank not complying with a freeze order`
    `s 7(3) failing to produce a document`
    `s 8(5) not complying with a s 8 order`
    `s 8(6) furnishing false information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 5 failing to disclose information` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 20000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `s 5 failing to disclose information` THEN 5
    WHEN `s 6(3) bank not complying with a freeze order` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 2

§§ `9 -- consent to prosecute`

-- s 9: "A prosecution under this Act must not be instituted except by or with the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `instituted by the Public Prosecutor` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the Public Prosecutor's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `instituted by the Public Prosecutor` OR `with the Public Prosecutor's consent`

§§ `10 -- protection of informers`

-- s 10(1): except as in (3), a witness "must not be obliged" to disclose an informer's name or address, or answer a question tending to
-- reveal it. (3) The court may require full disclosure if "(a) in any proceedings for an offence under this Act" it is satisfied the
-- informer "wilfully made a material statement which he or she knew or believed to be false or did not believe to be true"; or "(b)
-- in any other proceedings" it is of the opinion that "justice cannot be fully done between the parties" without disclosure.
-- So in a prosecution under this Act the justice ground is not available, and in other proceedings the false-statement ground is not.
GIVEN `proceedings for an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `informer wilfully made a false material statement` IS A BOOLEAN, `justice cannot be fully done without disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may require disclosure of the informer` IF
    IF `proceedings for an offence under this Act`
    THEN `informer wilfully made a false material statement`
    ELSE `justice cannot be fully done without disclosure`

§§ `11 -- officers, partners and members`

-- s 11(1), (3), (5): where an offence under this Act by a body corporate, partnership or unincorporated association is proved to have
-- been committed "with the consent or connivance" of an officer, partner or member, or to be "attributable to any act or default" on
-- their part, that person is also guilty. (4) For a limited liability partnership the second ground reads "attributable to any
-- neglect on the part of" a partner or manager.
DECLARE Entity IS ONE OF
    `a body corporate`
    `a partnership`
    `a limited liability partnership`
    `an unincorporated association`

GIVEN `the entity` IS AN Entity, `the entity's offence proved` IS A BOOLEAN, `with the individual's consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to the individual's act or default` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to the individual's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer, partner or member is also guilty` IF
        `the entity's offence proved`
    AND (    `with the individual's consent or connivance`
         OR  CONSIDER `the entity`
             WHEN `a limited liability partnership` THEN `attributable to the individual's neglect`
             OTHERWISE `attributable to the individual's act or default`)

§§ `12 -- arrest without warrant`

-- s 12: "A police officer may arrest without warrant any person whom he or she reasonably believes has committed an offence under this
-- Act." Every offence under the Act qualifies, including failure to disclose (s 5) and the document offences (ss 7, 8).
GIVEN `the officer reasonably believes an offence under this Act was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer may arrest without warrant` IF
    `the officer reasonably believes an offence under this Act was committed`

§§ `14(1) -- extradition`

-- s 14(1): "Every hostage-taking offence is deemed to be an extradition offence under the Extradition Act 1968." [Act 17 of 2022]
GIVEN `the involvement` IS AN Involvement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the involvement is deemed an extradition offence` IF
    `the involvement is a hostage-taking offence` `the involvement`
